                    {
                        "sense_id": "0fbf49f5-906d-3db5-9cde-478e4c2cee7b",
                        "entry_id": "1cbc25bf-67b7-34dd-a9ea-4f6509a8f4fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A woman who sews clothes professionally."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3da76bf-7f3b-404e-9e42-740ee13f2628",
                                "sense_id": "0fbf49f5-906d-3db5-9cde-478e4c2cee7b",
                                "text": "[…] the Seamſtreſs brought in her ſilver thimble, the Chamber-maid her Bodkin, the Cook his ſilver ſpoon, the Vintner his Bowl into the common Treaſury of War and they who contributed to ſo pious a work, were invited more then others in ſome Churches to come to the Holy Communion in the very time of adminiſtration; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c009b0f7-a300-4bee-88e8-1020c5608b1d",
                                "sense_id": "0fbf49f5-906d-3db5-9cde-478e4c2cee7b",
                                "text": "They are seamstresses, who have plied the daily and nightly needle in the service of master tailors and close-fisted contractors, until now it is almost time for each to hem the borders of her own shroud."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "086205aa-8164-4ddf-9a6e-c806236a3c7a",
                                "sense_id": "0fbf49f5-906d-3db5-9cde-478e4c2cee7b",
                                "text": "“If you have finished blathering about men, perhaps you won’t mind skipping over the new seamstress you’ve no doubt found?\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
